# Testing required

Every behavior change must ship with automated tests. Do not merge feature/fix work without updating or adding tests.

## Stack

| Layer | Tool | Location |
|-------|------|----------|
| API unit | Jest | `apps/api/src/**/*.spec.ts` |
| API HTTP | Jest + Supertest | `apps/api/test/**/*.e2e-spec.ts` |
| UI / flows | Playwright | `e2e/**/*.spec.ts` |

## Rules

- New API endpoints/services → unit tests + HTTP e2e when the route is user/contract facing
- New UI pages/flows/copy/i18n behavior → Playwright coverage for the happy path (and critical edge cases)
- Bug fixes → regression test that fails without the fix
- Refactors → keep existing tests green; add tests if behavior was previously untested
- Do not rely on manual clicking as the only verification
- Prefer focused tests over snapshot spam; use Playwright trace/screenshot on failure
- Bilingual UI assertions must cover **ru** and **en** when the change is user-facing copy or routing

## Commands

```bash
npm run test:api      # Jest unit
npm run test:api:e2e  # Jest API e2e
npm run test:e2e      # Playwright
npm test              # api unit + api e2e + playwright
```

## Examples

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — new health field covered
expect(service.getHealth()).toMatchObject({ status: 'ok' });

// ❌ BAD — ship /profiles UI with zero Playwright specs
```

When asked to implement a feature, include tests in the same change set unless the user explicitly says otherwise.
